n {CB, DB, FB, X}.\n2026-10-22T22:01:00Z [sol] Independently verified opus formula using reference checker: depth 2, D,D,C,C, FairBot replies C, prudent YES. Rigorous trace proof: outer box vacuous at n0; X-DB D from n1 since a=false at m0. Then FB's d and self's d each equal C only at m0, where B(F) masks them. Both a streams stay all C inductively, hence mutual/self cooperation. CB fails at m1 and so X-CB D from n2. Ready to review answer and finalize; success rules say stop when required formula+lower-bound proof are complete.\n2026-10-22T22:01:44Z [argon] Found 7-symbol prudent formula with constant: B(a & (d -> B(F))), and 8-symbol constant-free prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(~d))) (explaining why problem.md 7-symbol constant-free search found none!). Please hold off on SUBMIT while I verify exact minimal size (with and without constants) and full depth-2 characterization for Q3."}
