{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:01:55.730Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_258193","parameters":{"description":"Exhaustively search small formulas with and without constants to find minimum sizes","command":"python3 -c '\nimport check\n\nprint(\"Checking B(a & (d -> B(~d))):\", check.outcomes(\"B(a & (d -> B(~d)))\"))\n\n# Enumerate ASTs by symbol count (number of nodes in syntax tree over T,F,a,c,d, ~, B, &, |, ->)\n# Inside a box vs outside a box:\n# Wait: a formula is fully modalized iff every atom outside any box is only T or F, and inside a box can be T, F, a, c, d.\n# Instead of evaluating syntactically, we can evaluate truth tables or directly test with check.py!\n# Even better: let us generate formulas by size s = 1..8 and memoize by their semantic behavior or test directly.\n\ndef gen(size, inside, allow_const=True):\n    if size == 1:\n        if allow_const:\n            yield \"T\"\n            yield \"F\"\n        if inside:\n            yield \"a\"\n            yield \"c\"\n            yield \"d\"\n        return\n    # Unary: ~ and B\n    for sub in gen(size - 1, inside, allow_const):\n        yield f\"~({sub})\"\n    for sub in gen(size - 1, True, allow_const):\n        yield f\"B({sub})\"\n    # Binary: &, |, ->\n    for left_size in range(1, size - 1):\n        right_size = size - 1 - left_size\n        for l in gen(left_size, inside, allow_const):\n            for r in gen(right_size, inside, allow_const):\n                yield f\"({l}) & ({r})\"\n                yield f\"({l}) | ({r})\"\n                yield f\"({l}) -> ({r})\"\n\nfor allow_const in [True, False]:\n    max_s = 7 if allow_const else 8\n    print(f\"=== Search allow_const={allow_const}, up to size {max_s} ===\")\n    for s in range(1, max_s + 1):\n        found = []\n        count = 0\n        for f in gen(s, False, allow_const):\n            count += 1\n            d, r = check.outcomes(f, worlds=10)\n            if r[\"CB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"DB\"] == \"D\" and r[\"FB\"] == \"C\" and r[\"FB_reply\"] == \"C\" and r[\"X\"] == \"C\":\n                found.append(f)\n        print(f\"Size {s}: tested {count} formulas, found {len(found)} prudent\")\n        if found:\n            for ex in found[:10]:\n                print(\"  Example:\", ex)\n            break\n'"}}
