{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:02:54.229Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_228954","parameters":{"description":"Check unrestricted depth up to size 7 (with constants) and size 8 (without constants), and read board.md","command":"python3 -c '\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\ndef gen(size, inside, allow_const=True):\n    if size == 1:\n        if allow_const:\n            yield (\"T\",), \"T\"\n            yield (\"F\",), \"F\"\n        if inside:\n            yield (\"a\",), \"a\"\n            yield (\"c\",), \"c\"\n            yield (\"d\",), \"d\"\n        return\n    for ast, s in gen(size - 1, inside, allow_const):\n        yield (\"not\", ast), f\"~{s}\" if len(s) == 1 or s.startswith((\"B(\", \"(\", \"~\")) else f\"~({s})\"\n    for ast, s in gen(size - 1, True, allow_const):\n        yield (\"box\", ast), f\"B({s})\"\n    for left_size in range(1, size - 1):\n        right_size = size - 1 - left_size\n        for l_ast, l_s in gen(left_size, inside, allow_const):\n            for r_ast, r_s in gen(right_size, inside, allow_const):\n                yield (\"and\", l_ast, r_ast), f\"({l_s} & {r_s})\"\n                yield (\"or\", l_ast, r_ast), f\"({l_s} | {r_s})\"\n                yield (\"or\", (\"not\", l_ast), r_ast), f\"({l_s} -> {r_s})\"\n\ndef is_prudent(X, W=20):\n    agents = {\"CB\": (\"T\",), \"DB\": (\"F\",), \"FB\": (\"box\", (\"a\",)), \"X\": X}\n    @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n    def act(x, y, n):\n        return ev(agents[x], n, x, y)\n    def ev(f, n, me, opp):\n        t = f[0]\n        if t == \"T\": return True\n        if t == \"F\": return False\n        if t == \"a\": return act(opp, me, n)\n        if t == \"c\": return act(opp, \"CB\", n)\n        if t == \"d\": return act(opp, \"DB\", n)\n        if t == \"not\": return not ev(f[1], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"and\": return ev(f[1], n, me, opp) and ev(f[2], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"or\": return ev(f[1], n, me, opp) or ev(f[2], n, me, opp)\n        if t == \"box\": return all(ev(f[1], m, me, opp) for m in range(n))\n    if act(\"X\", \"CB\", W-1): return False\n    if act(\"X\", \"DB\", W-1): return False\n    if not act(\"X\", \"FB\", W-1): return False\n    if not act(\"FB\", \"X\", W-1): return False\n    if not act(\"X\", \"X\", W-1): return False\n    return True\n\nfor allow_const in [True, False]:\n    max_s = 7 if allow_const else 8\n    print(f\"=== UNRESTRICTED DEPTH allow_const={allow_const}, up to size {max_s} ===\")\n    for s in range(1, max_s + 1):\n        found = []\n        count = 0\n        for ast, f_str in gen(s, False, allow_const):\n            count += 1\n            if is_prudent(ast):\n                found.append(f_str)\n        print(f\"Size {s}: tested {count} formulas, found {len(found)} prudent\")\n        if found:\n            for ex in found:\n                print(\"  Example:\", ex)\n            break\n' && cat /work/board.md"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-10-22T22:03:07.717Z","tool_id":"run_shell_command__call_228954","status":"success","output":"=== UNRESTRICTED DEPTH allow_const=True, up to size 7 ===\nSize 1: tested 2 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 2: tested 7 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 3: tested 29 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 4: tested 208 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 5: tested 1193 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 6: tested 9037 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 7: tested 63272 formulas, found 2 prudent\n  Example: B((a & (d -> B(F))))\n  Example: B(((d -> B(F)) & a))\n=== UNRESTRICTED DEPTH allow_const=False, up to size 8 ===\nSize 1: tested 0 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 2: tested 3 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 3: tested 9 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 4: tested 48 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 5: tested 261 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 6: tested 1605 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 7: tested 9828 formulas, found 0 prudent\nSize 8: tested 63885 formulas, found 6 prudent\n  Example: B((a & (d -> B(~a))))\n  Example: B((a & (d -> B(~c))))\n  Example: B((a & (d -> B(~d))))\n  Example: B(((d -> B(~a)) & a))\n  Example: B(((d -> B(~c)) & a))\n  Example: B(((d -> B(~d)) & a))\n2026-10-22T22:00:07Z [sol] Reading semantics; I will investigate unrestricted depth-1 impossibility and report a structural proof. Please coordinate candidate depth-2/3 search independently.\n2026-10-22T22:00:17Z [sol] COMPLETE lower bound: for depth 1, X vs CB is constant from world 1 because opponent atoms always 111. Prudence forces this constant D. FairBot cooperation with X at stable worlds implies X vs FB was C at EVERY world (one D permanently falsifies FairBot's box). But at world 1 FB's a,c,d are all true at world 0, so every depth-1 fully modalized formula has identical X-vs-FB and X-vs-CB evaluations there. Contradiction. Depth 0 constants plainly fail. Thus minimal depth >=2. Will seek depth-2 construction unless others already assigned.\n2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [opus] Agree with sol's depth-1 proof (I derived the same). Depth-2 prudent agent verified by check.py: B(a & (B(F) | ~d)) (= PrudentBot, □(a ∧ (¬□⊥→¬d))). Also B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d). I'm writing answer.md now with DEPTH: 2 + proof; will look at minimal size for Q3. Others: please don't overwrite, append comments instead.\n2026-10-22T22:00:34Z [sol] FOUND depth-2 prudent candidate: B(a) & (B(B(F)) | ~B(d)). Checker next. Mechanism: CB C at n0,1 then D; DB C at n0 then D; FB/self always C. Together with my unrestricted depth-1 lower bound this solves required parts. I will write answer.md shortly unless another agent has draft ownership.\n2026-10-22T22:00:42Z [sol] Opus: your candidate is shorter (8 syntax-tree symbols counting each connective, box, atom, constant once) than mine (10). Agree you own answer.md; I will independently verify your candidate and inspect proof, not overwrite. Your candidate yields same traces CB C,C,D..., DB C,D..., FB/self C forever.\n2026-10-22T22:00:57Z [argon] Starting analysis of world-by-world valuation sequences v_Y(n) = (a,c,d) for Y in {CB, DB, FB, X}.\n2026-10-22T22:01:00Z [sol] Independently verified opus formula using reference checker: depth 2, D,D,C,C, FairBot replies C, prudent YES. Rigorous trace proof: outer box vacuous at n0; X-DB D from n1 since a=false at m0. Then FB's d and self's d each equal C only at m0, where B(F) masks them. Both a streams stay all C inductively, hence mutual/self cooperation. CB fails at m1 and so X-CB D from n2. Ready to review answer and finalize; success rules say stop when required formula+lower-bound proof are complete.\n2026-10-22T22:01:44Z [argon] Found 7-symbol prudent formula with constant: B(a & (d -> B(F))), and 8-symbol constant-free prudent formula: B(a & (d -> B(~d))) (explaining why problem.md 7-symbol constant-free search found none!). Please hold off on SUBMIT while I verify exact minimal size (with and without constants) and full depth-2 characterization for Q3.\n2026-10-22T22:02:00Z [opus] answer.md written (FORMULA B(a & (d -> B(F))), DEPTH 2, depth<=1 proof, Q3 enumeration: size-7 minimal by AST nodes, unique class; size-8 list). sol/argon: review & append objections within a few min; otherwise I'll mark FINAL and write SUBMIT.\n2026-10-22T22:02:03Z [sol] Argon's 7-symbol implication form independently verified prudent. It is propositionally identical to opus formula. With primitive -> its size is 7: B,a,&,d,->,B,F. I remain available for review, have not written SUBMIT.\n2026-10-22T22:02:40Z [sol] REVIEW PASSED: answer.md construction, exact world traces, unrestricted depth<=1 proof all correct. Q3 properly labels heuristic enumeration as evidence; 7-node upper bound is rigorous. General boxed-theta sufficient family is valid because outer a forces X-DB false at all n>=1, regardless theta. I agree answer content and consider core answer final. [sol] FINAL\n2026-10-22T22:02:44Z [sol] Opus: no objections; you may submit once argon's review arrives. I will ensure SUBMIT exists before ending my turn."}
